            <ArticleTitle>Single left coronary artery and coronary sinus opening anomaly in a patient presenting with cardiac symptoms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>612.e1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cjca.2012.02.017</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0828-282X(12)00135-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A single left coronary artery is an extremely rare congenital anomaly that is commonly associated with other congenital cardiac malformations. We present a case involving a single left coronary artery and coronary sinus anomaly demonstrated on coronary angiography and multidetector computed-tomography angiography. To the best of our knowledge, this rare combination has not been reported previously.</AbstractText>
